namespace Death {
//###==##====#=====--==~--~=~- --- -- -  -  -   -

/** @page amiga Building the project for Amiga systems
@brief Guide how to build, deploy and run Jazz² Resurrection on AmigaOS 3.x, AmigaOS 4.1 and MorphOS

@tableofcontents

@m_class{m-noindent}

None of the three supported Amiga systems has graphics hardware the game's shader pipeline can use.
Classic machines render with the CPU `Software` rasterizer. The two PowerPC systems use the
fixed-function `LegacyGL` backend @m_span{m-text m-dim} (TinyGL on MorphOS, MiniGL over Warp3D on
AmigaOS 4, see @ref amiga-morphos-gl) @m_endspan by default, with `Software` still selectable for a
card without a 3D driver.

System | Toolchain @m_span{m-text m-dim} (CMake toolchain file) @m_endspan | Renderer | Window/input | Audio | Details
------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------ | ----- | -------
AmigaOS 3.x @m_span{m-text m-dim} (m68k) @m_endspan | AmigaPorts' m68k-amigaos-gcc @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`amiga.cmake`) @m_endspan | `Software` | own backend @m_span{m-text m-dim} (Intuition + RTG) @m_endspan | `AHI` | @ref amiga-classic
AmigaOS 4.1 @m_span{m-text m-dim} (PowerPC) @m_endspan | adtools @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`os4.cmake`) @m_endspan | `LegacyGL` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (MiniGL) @m_endspan | SDL2 | OpenAL or `SDL` | @ref amiga-os4
MorphOS @m_span{m-text m-dim} (PowerPC) @m_endspan | MorphOS SDK @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`morphos.cmake`) @m_endspan | `LegacyGL` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (TinyGL) @m_endspan | SDL2 | `SDL` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (OpenAL if built) @m_endspan | @ref amiga-morphos

@m_class{m-noindent}

The design document, including the hardware research behind the classic port, is
`Docs/AmigaPortDesign.md`.

@section amiga-classic AmigaOS 3.x (m68k)

One executable covers PiStorm/Emu68, Apollo Vampire and 68060 machines with an RTG card. It presents
into a Picasso96/CyberGraphX chunky framebuffer. The amount of work is chosen at startup by measuring
the machine, see @ref amiga-presets.

Property | Value
-------- | -----
Toolchain | AmigaPorts' <b>m68k-amigaos-gcc</b> @m_span{m-text m-dim} (GCC 16.2 prebuilt, `cmake/toolchains/amiga.cmake`) @m_endspan
C runtime | libnix @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`-mcrt=nix20`) @m_endspan
Rendering backend | `Software`, 16-bit surfaces @m_span{m-text m-dim} (any other value is a configure error) @m_endspan
Window/input backend | `Amiga` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Sources/nCine/Backends/Amiga/`) @m_endspan: Intuition screen, IDCMP input, lowlevel.library gamepads
Audio backend | `AHI` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Sources/nCine/Audio/Backends/Amiga/`) @m_endspan: software mixer into `ahi.device`
Music | libxmp @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`NCINE_WITH_XMP`, downloaded and built by CMake configure) @m_endspan, reads `.j2b` directly
Build artifact | `build/amiga/dist/`: `Jazz2` executable + `Content/`

@subsection amiga-hardware What it runs on

Machine | Verdict
------- | -------
PiStorm / Emu68 @m_span{m-text m-dim} (Pi3A+, CM4, Pi4) @m_endspan | <b>Primary target.</b>
Apollo Vampire V4 / V1200 @m_span{m-text m-dim} (68080 + SAGA) @m_endspan | Supported, AMMX kernels enabled automatically. Expect reduced settings.
68060 + RTG card @m_span{m-text m-dim} (Picasso IV, ZZ9000, …) @m_endspan | The floor: `Low` preset, experimental.
68030/68040, or no FPU | Not supported: refuses to start without an FPU.
Stock AGA @m_span{m-text m-dim} (no RTG) @m_endspan | Not supported.

@m_class{m-noindent}

An RTG screen mode is required. Plan for at least 8 MB of fast RAM.

@subsection amiga-toolchain Toolchain

Use the prebuilt, relocatable [AmigaPorts/m68k-amigaos-gcc](https://github.com/AmigaPorts/m68k-amigaos-gcc)
release @m_span{m-text m-dim} (Linux x86_64, macOS arm64) @m_endspan. GCC 13 is the minimum.

@code{.sh}
# The archive's directory is the prefix; unpack it anywhere
curl -fsSLO https://github.com/AmigaPorts/m68k-amigaos-gcc/releases/download/v16.2-rc10/m68k-amigaos-gcc-16.2-rc10-x86_64-linux.tar.xz
tar xJf m68k-amigaos-gcc-16.2-rc10-x86_64-linux.tar.xz -C /opt
export AMIGA_INST=/opt/m68k-amigaos-gcc-16.2
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

The release already contains everything needed: NDK 3.2, the CyberGraphX and AHI headers, vasm
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`vasmm68k_mot`, needed only for `NCINE_WITH_AMMX`) @m_endspan and zlib 1.3.2 for
every multilib.

@m_class{m-block m-info}

@par Don't rebuild zlib
zlib 1.3.2's `configure` aborts because `m68k-amigaos-gcc` rejects `-fPIC`. If you build a replacement
anyway, set `AR` and `RANLIB` explicitly: the host `ranlib` writes an index `m68k-amigaos-ld` can't
read, and the link then fails on `crc32`, `inflate*` and `deflate*`.

@subsubsection amiga-toolchain-flags Flags in the toolchain file that must stay

<ul>
<li>`-mcpu=68060` <b>with</b> `-m68881`: the CPU flag alone means soft-float, which makes all float
math libgcc calls and makes the hard-float libnix `libm` @m_span{m-text m-dim}
(`libm020/libm881/libm.a`) @m_endspan return garbage from `fminf()`, `fmaxf()`, `rint()`,
`nearbyint()`. @m_span{m-text m-dim} `-print-multi-directory` printing `.` for this combination is
harmless. @m_endspan</li>
<li>`-fno-optimize-sibling-calls` is required for correctness: binutils resolves tail calls to weak
symbols to the wrong address. `-fno-weak` is not an alternative, it breaks linking of template statics
such as `Vector2f::Zero`.</li>
<li>`-std=gnu++17` is pinned because GCC 16 defaults to C++20, where `<math.h>` brings `std::lerp`
into the global namespace and clashes with `nCine::lerp`.</li>
</ul>

@m_class{m-noindent}

It also force-includes `cmake/toolchains/amiga-libstdc++-c99.h` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (as on PS3)
@m_endspan, because this libstdc++ lacks `_GLIBCXX_USE_C99_MATH_TR1` and `<cmath>` declares no C99 math
in `std::`.

@subsection amiga-content Preparing the content tree

`Source` and `Cache` sit next to the executable, so an original <em>Jazz Jackrabbit 2</em> copied into
`Source` is converted on first start, but that is very slow on a 68060. Normally point the build at a
tree prebaked on the host with @ref asset-packer "AssetPacker":

@code{.sh}
cmake -B ./build/amiga/ -D CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=./cmake/toolchains/amiga.cmake \
    -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -D NCINE_CONTENT_DIR=./build/ConsoleContent
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

With `NCINE_CONTENT_DIR` pointing at the repository's `Content` instead, only base assets are included
and the game shows "content missing" until an original installation is placed in `Source`.

@subsection amiga-build Building

@code{.sh}
export AMIGA_INST=/opt/amiga
export PATH="$AMIGA_INST/bin:$PATH"

cmake -B ./build/amiga/ -D CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=./cmake/toolchains/amiga.cmake \
    -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -D NCINE_CONTENT_DIR=./build/ConsoleContent
cmake --build ./build/amiga/ --parallel $(nproc)
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

`AMIGA_INST` is the toolchain prefix. Configure fails unless `$AMIGA_INST/bin/m68k-amigaos-gcc`, the
NDK headers and zlib are there @m_span{m-text m-dim} (see @ref amiga-toolchain) @m_endspan. The
`AmigaOS 3.x` job in `.github/workflows/amiga.yml` runs the same recipe unattended.

Copy `build/amiga/dist/` to the Amiga. `Jazz2.config` is written into the same directory.

<ul>
<li>Link-time optimization is off @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`NCINE_LINKTIME_OPTIMIZATION`) @m_endspan and
Release uses `-O2`, not `-O3`.</li>
<li>Threads are off @m_span{m-text m-dim} (no `std::thread` on m68k-amigaos) @m_endspan: everything,
including audio decoding, runs on the main thread.</li>
</ul>

@subsection amiga-deploy Deploying and running

Copy `dist/` anywhere on a hard drive and run it from a Shell or its icon. It opens its own screen. The
1 MB stack comes from the executable's `__stack` cookie, so `Stack` isn't needed
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Stack 1048576` in a script does no harm) @m_endspan.

For development, use <b>FS-UAE with AROS 68k</b> (ships CyberGraphX and AHI):

@code{.ini}
# jazz2.fs-uae
amiga_model = A4000
cpu = 68040
jit_compiler = 0
kickstart_file = /path/to/aros/boot/amiga/aros-rom.bin
hard_drive_0 = /path/to/aros/dh0
hard_drive_1 = /path/to/jazz2/build/amiga/dist
@endcode

@m_class{m-block m-warning}

@par AROS pitfalls
<ul>
<li>The ROM hangs before video with `cpu = 68060` or the JIT on: use 68040 and `jit_compiler = 0`.</li>
<li>No sound at all until you add `C:AddAudioModes DEVS:AudioModes/PAULA` to `S/User-Startup`
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (patterns like `#?` don't work here) @m_endspan.</li>
<li>FS-UAE's `kickstart_file = internal` AROS is too old to boot a current AROS installation.</li>
</ul>

@m_class{m-noindent}

The log goes to stdout unbuffered, so redirect it to keep a full trace across crashes. A
`-DDEATH_DEBUG=ON` build also accepts `/level <episode>/<level>` to boot straight into a level:

@code
Jazz2:Jazz2 >Jazz2:jazz2-log.txt
Jazz2:Jazz2 /level prince/castle1 >Jazz2:jazz2-log.txt
@endcode

@subsection amiga-presets Performance presets and autodetection

At startup `AmigaPlatform::RunPerformanceProbe()` times a 16-bit blend loop and an FPU chain and picks
a preset:

Preset | Pixel budget | Mixing rate
------ | ------------ | -----------
`Ultra` | 640×512 | 44100 Hz
`High` | 640×360 | 44100 Hz
`Medium` | 384×300 | 22050 Hz
`Low` | 320×220 | 22050 Hz

@m_class{m-noindent}

The RTG mode chosen is the one with the largest <em>logical</em> resolution @m_span{m-text m-dim}
(720×405-clamped aspect fit) @m_endspan within the budget, so 640×400 can win over 640×480. The probe
prints `… ns/composited pixel, … ns/FPU multiply-add` to the log on every boot. Under emulation use it
only to compare two builds, never as an absolute figure.

Variable | Effect
-------- | ------
`NCINE_PRESET` | `low`, `medium`, `high` or `ultra`: forces the preset.
`NCINE_NO_AMMX` | Any value: use the scalar kernels on an Apollo 68080 @m_span{m-text m-dim} (diagnostic only, output is bit-identical) @m_endspan.

@subsection amiga-limits Limits and known issues

<ul>
<li><b>FPU required.</b> Without one the game exits with a message. On a 68040/68060 `Libs:68040.library`
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (resp. `68060.library`) @m_endspan must be installed for `SetPatch`. Bare
Workbench 3.1 lacks it and fails with `Recoverable Alert 0006 8881`. The 68080 and Emu68 need
nothing.</li>
<li><b>RTG only</b>, no chunky-to-planar path.</li>
<li><b>No threads</b> (`WITH_THREADS` off): audio streaming decodes on the main thread and multiplayer
client/server aren't built.</li>
<li><b>Music is libxmp</b> @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`cmake/Findlibxmp.cmake`) @m_endspan: it can't read
MO3, so the four `.mo3` tracks are silent @m_span{m-text m-dim} (as on PSP, see
@ref consoles-psp-limits) @m_endspan.</li>
<li><b>`ahi.device` queueing differs</b> between implementations @m_span{m-text m-dim} (AROS 68k never
plays `ahir_Link` requests and stalls a drained queue) @m_endspan. The backend detects linking at
startup and restarts a queue idle for a second. The `Audio device initialized: …` log line shows the
mode.</li>
<li><b>libnix gaps</b>: `exp2`, `exp2f`, `log2f`, `strnlen`, `wcstoul`, `flock`, `fchmod`, `getpwuid`,
`realpath`, `gethostname` and `__xpg_strerror_r` are provided by
`Sources/nCine/Backends/Amiga/AmigaLibcCompat.c`. Don't add replacements for `round`, `trunc`, `fmin`,
`fmax`, `rint` or `nearbyint`, because libnix's are correct with hard-float
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (see @ref amiga-toolchain-flags) @m_endspan.</li>
</ul>

@section amiga-os4 AmigaOS 4.1 (PowerPC)

Window and input use the desktop SDL2 backend. Audio is OpenAL Soft @m_span{m-text m-dim} (AHI
backend, linked statically, and the SDK's `libopenal.so` is ignored) @m_endspan when the toolchain image
carries it @m_span{m-text m-dim} (images from October 2026 on) @m_endspan, otherwise the `SDL` backend
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Sources/nCine/Audio/Backends/SDL/`, software mixer into `SDL_QueueAudio()`)
@m_endspan. `-D CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_OpenAL=ON` forces the `SDL` fallback.

@subsection amiga-os4-gl Hardware rendering through MiniGL

The renderer is `LegacyGL` on <b>MiniGL</b> @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`libGL.a` + `minigl.library`)
@m_endspan, the same backend as MorphOS (see @ref amiga-morphos-gl), with two differences:

<ul>
<li>MiniGL has `GL_EXT_texture_env_combine` but <b>no framebuffer objects</b>, so the copy-back
render-target path is compiled in and FBOs compiled out @m_span{m-text m-dim}
(`RHI_LEGACYGL_HAS_FBO` in `LegacyGlApi.h`) @m_endspan.</li>
<li>No mirrored repeat: that wrap mode degrades to plain repeat.</li>
</ul>

@m_class{m-noindent}

Warp3D Nova's `ogles2.library` would fit the ES2 profile @m_span{m-text m-dim}
(`NCINE_RHI_GL_PROFILE=ES2`) @m_endspan, but the SDK has no GLES2 headers or link library for it. Use
`-D NCINE_PREFERRED_RHI=Software` on a machine with no 3D driver.

@subsection amiga-os4-build Toolchain and building

adtools @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`ppc-amigaos-gcc` 11.5) @m_endspan and the AmigaOS 4.1 SDK come in one
container image. Mount the repository at its own path:

@code{.sh}
docker run --rm -v "$PWD:$PWD" -w "$PWD" docker.io/walkero/amigagccondocker:os4-gcc11 bash -lc '
    cmake -B ./build/os4/ -D CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=./cmake/toolchains/os4.cmake \
        -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -D NCINE_CONTENT_DIR=./build/ConsoleContent
    cmake --build ./build/os4/ --parallel $(nproc)'
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

<ul>
<li>Podman takes the same arguments. Add `--security-opt label=disable` under enforcing SELinux.</li>
<li>The adtools prefix defaults to `/opt/ppc-amigaos`. Set `OS4_INST` to use a host installation.</li>
<li>Output: `build/os4/dist/` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Jazz2` + `Content/`, stripped) @m_endspan.</li>
<li>CI: the container job in `.github/workflows/amiga.yml`.</li>
</ul>

@subsection amiga-os4-limits What differs from a desktop build

<ul>
<li><b>No online multiplayer</b>: the SDK's bsdsocket has no IPv6 (ENet needs it) and no `<poll.h>`
(IXWebSocket needs it). Local splitscreen works.</li>
<li><b>Threads are on</b>, using `-athread=native` + the SDK's `libpthread`
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`-athread=pthread` can't be used: `gthr-amigaos-pthread.o` isn't shipped)
@m_endspan. Thread affinity, names, barriers and `pthread_kill()` are compiled out.</li>
<li>`libatomic` is linked explicitly for 64-bit atomics on 32-bit PowerPC.</li>
<li>Keep `-Uamiga` in the machine flags: the predefined lowercase `amiga` macro breaks identifiers such
as libopenmpt's `common_encoding::amiga`.</li>
</ul>

@section amiga-morphos MorphOS (PowerPC)

Same setup as AmigaOS 4: SDL2 window/input, `SDL` audio and `LegacyGL` on TinyGL
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (@ref amiga-morphos-gl) @m_endspan, with a different toolchain and its own quirks.

@subsection amiga-morphos-build Toolchain and building

The MorphOS SDK @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`ppc-morphos-gcc` 11.3, at `/gg`) @m_endspan is a container
image too. It ships <b>no zlib</b>, which the game requires, so build it first:

@code{.sh}
docker run --rm -v "$PWD:$PWD" -w "$PWD" -e MORPHOS_DEPS=/tmp/morphos-deps \
    docker.io/walkero/amigagccondocker:mos-gcc-amd64 bash -lc '
    curl -fsSL https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/download/v1.3.1/zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz | tar xz -C /tmp
    cd /tmp/zlib-1.3.1
    CC=ppc-morphos-gcc CFLAGS="-O2 -noixemul" ./configure --prefix=$MORPHOS_DEPS --static
    make -j $(nproc) libz.a && make install

    cd '"$PWD"'
    cmake -B ./build/morphos/ -D CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=./cmake/toolchains/morphos.cmake \
        -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -D NCINE_CONTENT_DIR=./build/ConsoleContent
    cmake --build ./build/morphos/ --parallel $(nproc)'
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

`MORPHOS_DEPS` is where the toolchain file finds cross-compiled dependencies. `MORPHOS_SDK` points at
an SDK outside `/gg`. Output goes to `build/morphos/dist/`. CI runs the same steps in
`.github/workflows/amiga.yml`.

For OpenAL audio, cross-compile BSzili's openal-soft port @m_span{m-text m-dim} (from its sources on
MorphOS Storage, not the prebuilt library, which targets an older C runtime) @m_endspan into
`MORPHOS_DEPS` before configuring. Otherwise the `SDL` backend is used.

@subsection amiga-morphos-run Running it

Install <b>`sdl2.library`</b> into `LIBS:` @m_span{m-text m-dim} ("SDL 2.32.11 Libraries" on MorphOS
Storage) @m_endspan. The SDK's `libSDL2.a` is only a stub and without the library the loader stops the
game before `main()`. No TCP/IP stack is needed.

Without hardware, QEMU's Pegasos II boots the MorphOS ISO:

@code{.sh}
# boot.img is extracted from the top level of the MorphOS ISO
qemu-system-ppc -machine pegasos2 -m 1024 -rtc base=localtime     -device ati-vga,romfile="" -cdrom morphos-3.20.iso -kernel boot.img -serial stdio
@endcode

@m_class{m-block m-info}

@par Driving it headlessly
Add `-display none -serial file:serial.log -qmp unix:qmp.sock,server,nowait`. Take screenshots with
QMP `screendump`, and start the game with output redirected to `DEBUG:` to get its log in
`serial.log`. The live CD blocks on an `IPrefs` language requester, so automation must hook in before
`IPrefs` and assign `LIBS:` and `FONTS:` by hand. A remastered ISO only boots with System Id `MORPHOS`
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`xorriso -as mkisofs -sysid MORPHOS -V MorphOSBoot …`) @m_endspan.

@subsection amiga-morphos-gl Hardware rendering through TinyGL

<b>TinyGL</b> @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`tinygl.library`, on Radeon, Voodoo and Permedia cards) @m_endspan
is OpenGL 1.x with 1.3 combiners, FBOs and vertex arrays but no shaders. `LegacyGL`
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Sources/nCine/Graphics/RHI/LegacyGL/`) @m_endspan is the default on both
PowerPC Amigas. For a card without a 3D driver use the CPU rasterizer:

@code{.sh}
cmake -B ./build/morphos/ -D CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=./cmake/toolchains/morphos.cmake \
    -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -D NCINE_PREFERRED_RHI=Software
@endcode

@m_class{m-noindent}

Like the Dreamcast and PSP backends, it uses the transpiled `fixed_function` effects
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (`Shaders/Generated/LegacyGlGeneratedEffects.h`) @m_endspan as `GL_COMBINE`
programs and runs the <em>direct tier</em>: the scene goes straight to the display at logical
resolution with the CPU lightmap composited by the device.

<ul>
<li><b>Indexed textures are baked</b> through their palette row into RGBA8 before upload
@m_span{m-text m-dim} (no `GL_EXT_paletted_texture`) @m_endspan.</li>
<li><b>Power-of-two padding</b> is used where NPOT isn't supported. NPOT support and
`GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE` @m_span{m-text m-dim} (capped at 2048) @m_endspan are probed at startup. Tileset
atlases are 15 tiles wide in 512-texel chunks. Larger prebaked textures are split into pages.
`NCINE_NO_NPOT` forces padding.</li>
<li><b>Render targets</b> use an FBO if one works at startup, otherwise draw into the back buffer and
copy with `glCopyTexSubImage2D()`. `NCINE_NO_FBO` forces the copy path.</li>
</ul>

@m_class{m-block m-warning}

@par Not runnable under emulation
`LegacyGL` can't start under QEMU: the emulated ATI card fails `Radeon DMA` init, so `tinygl.library`
is unavailable and the loader stops the program. <b>Build with `-D NCINE_PREFERRED_RHI=Software` for
the emulator.</b> To develop `LegacyGL` itself, use `cmake -DNCINE_PREFERRED_RHI=LegacyGL` on desktop
Linux/Windows, which runs the same combiner pipeline.

@subsection amiga-morphos-limits What differs from a desktop build

The SDK's old Amiga headers clash with C++. The workarounds live in `cmake/toolchains/morphos.cmake`
and `cmake/toolchains/morphos-compat.h`:

<ul>
<li><b>`_NO_PPCINLINE` is defined</b> because the `ppcinline` macros (e.g. `bind`) rewrite
`std::bind` in libstdc++. `morphos-compat.h` declares what that leaves out @m_span{m-text m-dim}
(e.g. `bzero` for `FD_ZERO`) @m_endspan.</li>
<li><b>`proto/exec.h` and `proto/usergroup.h` are skipped</b> via their include guards, since their
global `struct Task` makes the engine's `Task<...>` ambiguous. `FindTask()` (for `getpid()`) is
declared by hand with an opaque return type.</li>
<li><b>Threads are off</b>: `<pthread.h>` brings `struct Task` back, so the port is single-threaded.</li>
<li>`__STDC_LIMIT_MACROS` is defined to get `INT32_MIN` and friends.</li>
<li>`realpath()`, `fsync()` and `flock()` are compiled out, while `wcstoul` and
`__throw_bad_array_new_length` are provided in `Sources/nCine/Backends/MorphOS/MorphOSLibcCompat.cpp`.</li>
<li><b>TinyGL globals</b> `TinyGLBase` and `__tglContext` must live in the program: the link forces
`-u _CSTP_init_TinyGLBase`, and `Sources/nCine/Backends/MorphOS/MorphOSTinyGl.cpp` points
`__tglContext` at the `SDL_GL_CreateContext()` context.</li>
<li><b>No `gethostname()`, `getpwuid()` or libcurl</b>: any reference to `bsdsocket.library` or
`usergroup.library` would stop the game from starting without a TCP/IP stack. So there is no update
check, and no online multiplayer.</li>
</ul>

@m_class{m-block m-warning}

@par Test status
MorphOS with `Software` runs under QEMU @m_span{m-text m-dim} (content, SDL2 window, 44.1 kHz audio,
menu) @m_endspan. `LegacyGL` builds for both PowerPC systems and is verified on desktop OpenGL, but has
not run on either. AmigaOS 4 has not been run at all @m_span{m-text m-dim} (QEMU's `sam460ex`/`amigaone`
can, given the commercial install media) @m_endspan. Treat both PowerPC ports as untested.

*/

}
